Other compliance / practical notes
- The home‑office deduction is allowed only if the space is used regularly and exclusively for business. Keep measurement and rent records, photos, and documentation of expenses.
- The home‑office actual method reduces net profit and therefore reduces SE tax; however the deduction cannot create a net loss for your business for the year if the home office is for a sole proprietorship with no passive losses.
- Keep receipts for the $2,000 donation (acknowledgment from the charity) in case of audit.
