7) Which deduction route to take (itemize vs standard)
- Based on the amounts you provided, you will almost certainly take the standard deduction ($20,800) for 2023.
- Home-office and self-employment expenses reduce your Schedule C net profit — they are business deductions, not Schedule A itemized deductions, so they help lower taxable income even if you take the standard deduction.

8) Forms you’ll likely need
- Form 1040 (main return)
- Schedule 1 (additional income and adjustments, e.g., half of SE tax, student loan interest if allowed)
- Schedule B (interest) — because taxable interest > $1,500
- Schedule C (report consulting income and business expenses)
- Schedule SE (self-employment tax)
