- Total gross income (approx): 82,350 + 15,000 + 1,975 = 99,325.
- Home office simplified: $700. Actual (rent portion only): ≈ $5,116.
- If you claim the actual home office portion of rent alone, that reduces your net self‑employment taxable profit and thus reduces income tax and SE tax — making the actual method frequently more beneficial.
- With total income around $99k, you are likely above the $90k student loan interest phaseout threshold, so that $2,700 may not be allowed. But the half SE tax and home office/business deductions reduce AGI and could affect eligibility — we should compute precisely.

