- Home office: if the space qualifies, you can deduct the business portion of your rent/utilities (actual method) or use the simplified method ($5/sq ft up to 300 sq ft). For your numbers the actual method looks substantially better (see calculation).

Home‑office deduction (details and quick math)
- Requirement: used regularly and exclusively for business, and it must be for your self‑employment activity (your consulting). If the 140 sq ft is used only for the consulting, it qualifies.
- Two methods:
  1) Simplified: $5 × 140 sq ft = $700 (no Form 8829 needed).
